<title>USA: Lightbridge, Intelligroup boost terms of IPOs.</title>
<headline>Lightbridge, Intelligroup boost terms of IPOs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lightbridge and Intelligroup Inc both increased the number of shares to be offered in upcoming initial public offerings, a spokesman for underwriter Cowen &amp; Co said.</p>
<p>Lightbridge will offer 3.8 million shares in an estimated price range of $8 to $10 each. It originally filed to offer 3.2 million shares.</p>
<p>Intelligroup, a software company based in Edison, N.J., will offer 2.475 million shares, up from 2.25 million, in an estimated range of $8 to $10 each.</p>
</text>
